From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Nicola Nicodemo <nicola084@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 5 Oct 2026 11:58:55 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] usb: typec: samsung-emuec: wake for a charger
 plugged in during sleep

With event handling quiesced across system sleep, a charger plugged in
while the lid is closed is only negotiated at the next resume, so the
battery runs down although a charger is connected.

While quiesced, arm the masked interrupt as a wake source on a port that
had nothing attached at suspend. A plug-in then wakes the system, the
port is resynced at PM_POST_SUSPEND (PD contract), and userspace
suspends again with the lid closed. Ports with something attached stay
unarmed, so a charger unplugged during sleep is still left alone until
resume.

Tested on a Galaxy Book4 Edge 14" (Fedora, KDE, lid-close suspend): ten
minutes asleep on battery without a spurious wake; a plug-in wakes, 20 V
is negotiated and the machine sleeps again within about 15 seconds,
charging; an unplug during sleep, alone or after such a plug-in, does
not wake or reset it.

Signed-off-by: Nicola Nicodemo <nicola084@gmail.com>
[birk: rebased onto antheas's samsung-emuec at 00dbccf779]
Signed-off-by: Birk Skyum <birk.skyum@pm.me>
---
 drivers/usb/typec/samsung-emuec.c | 20 +++++++++++++++++++-
 1 file changed, 19 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/drivers/usb/typec/samsung-emuec.c b/drivers/usb/typec/samsung-emuec.c
index 5ce664aed..81de81eda 100644
--- a/drivers/usb/typec/samsung-emuec.c
+++ b/drivers/usb/typec/samsung-emuec.c
@@ -112,6 +112,7 @@ struct samsung_emuec {
 	u32 requested_pdo;
 	struct notifier_block pm_nb;
 	bool quiesced;
+	bool wake_armed;
 };
 
 static int samsung_emuec_pm_notify(struct notifier_block *nb,
@@ -1148,11 +1149,26 @@ static int samsung_emuec_pm_notify(struct notifier_block *nb,
 		disable_irq(pdic->client->irq);	/* waits for a running handler */
 		cancel_delayed_work_sync(&pdic->work);
 		flush_work(&pdic->hpd_work);
-		dev_info(dev, "pm: quiesced (attached=%d)\n", pdic->attached);
+		/*
+		 * A charger plugged into an empty port during sleep is otherwise
+		 * negotiated only after the next resume: wake for it. The wake
+		 * stays off on an attached port, so an unplug during sleep is
+		 * still left alone until resume (the reset this quiescing fixes).
+		 * The masked interrupt still wakes: the msm GPIO irqchip enables
+		 * wake-armed lines on suspend.
+		 */
+		if (!pdic->attached && !enable_irq_wake(pdic->client->irq))
+			pdic->wake_armed = true;
+		dev_info(dev, "pm: quiesced (attached=%d wake=%d)\n",
+			 pdic->attached, pdic->wake_armed);
 		break;
 	case PM_POST_SUSPEND:
 		if (!pdic->quiesced)
 			break;
+		if (pdic->wake_armed) {
+			disable_irq_wake(pdic->client->irq);
+			pdic->wake_armed = false;
+		}
 		scoped_guard(mutex, &pdic->lock)
 			pdic->quiesced = false;
 		enable_irq(pdic->client->irq);
@@ -1169,6 +1185,8 @@ static void samsung_emuec_remove(struct i2c_client *client)
 	struct samsung_emuec *pdic = i2c_get_clientdata(client);
 
 	unregister_pm_notifier(&pdic->pm_nb);
+	if (pdic->wake_armed)
+		disable_irq_wake(client->irq);
 	if (pdic->quiesced)
 		enable_irq(client->irq);
 
